Companies are abandoning their core business identity and shoehorning AI solutions because competitors announced something or a headline demanded it — implementing AI as an end in itself rather than as an amplifier of what already makes them valuable. The result is sub-optimal deployments, security exposure, and workforce resistance, all while the company drifts away from the DNA that built them.

